// DRAFT. Not applied. Route 2 of docs/adr/0002-ios-builds-on-the-mac.md: Jorah's iOS tools
// (plugins/jorah-ios, issue 9) call the runner on the Mac (services/ios-runner, issue 8) over the
// tailnet, under contract docs/contracts/jorah-ios-v1.md. ADR 0002 accepted 2026-11-12 (D1 route 2,
// D2 waiver accepted). Apply only on Adam's yes, after the plugin is installed on the PC
// (`plugins install --link /opt/jorah/plugins/jorah-ios`, the way scripts/pc/install-github.sh
// installs jorah-github). Main's tool allow list is the separate ios-tools.patch.json5, applied after this.
//
// gateway.nodes is deliberately NOT here: no node, pluginTools.enabled stays false, system.run
// stays denied. If a dry run shows any gateway.nodes update, stop.
//
// Dry run: not run. It can't be yet: the plugin isn't installed, so plugins.entries.jorah-ios
// would fail validation, and this session doesn't touch the live Gateway. On the PC:
//   openclaw --profile jorah config patch --file /opt/jorah/config/pc/ios.patch.json5 --dry-run
// Expected: "Dry run successful" with updates only under plugins.allow and
// plugins.entries.jorah-ios; nothing under gateway.* or agents.*. Plugin config reloads without a
// Gateway restart (docs gateway/configuration/hot-reload.md, "Plugin config").
//
// Merge patch: arrays are replaced whole. plugins.allow is copied from github.patch.json5 on main
// plus jorah-ios. Before the dry run, compare it with `config get plugins.allow` on the PC and add
// anything applied since (jorah-guard, if P5 has enabled it by then); leaving an entry out
// removes that plugin.
//
// jorah-guard (P5) blocks every tool that isn't in config/permission-matrix.json. Before the tools
// can run, the matrix needs ios_build, ios_install and ios_status under "taintRead" (their results
// repeat repo content; still blocked while Jorah is frozen; the card comes from this plugin, so the
// guard adds none). That edit belongs to the P5 owner of the matrix.
//
// Tools and fields: ios_install also takes { simulator, action, project } since 2026-11-12 (contract
// 1, "On a simulator"); the tool names are unchanged, so ios-tools.patch.json5 is unchanged.
//
// Undo: github.patch.json5 (plugins.allow without jorah-ios) and `plugins.entries.jorah-ios: null`.
{
  plugins: {
    allow: [
      "anthropic",
      "telegram",
      "acpx",
      "memory-core",
      "active-memory",
      "memory-wiki",
      "device-pair",
      "talk-voice",
      "browser",
      "duckduckgo",
      "jorah-voice-provider",
      "jorah-github",
      "jorah-ios",
    ],
    entries: {
      "jorah-ios": {
        config: {
          // The Mac's MagicDNS name, filled on the PC. Tailnet TCP 47820, forwarded by Serve.
          runnerUrl: "http://<mac MagicDNS name>:47820",
          // Shared HMAC key, mode 600, made by Adam (contract section 4). Read per call. Never the key itself.
          keyFile: "/home/jorah/.config/jorah-ios/runner.key",
          // For early refusal and card text only. The runner's own allowlist decides.
          projects: ["threadfolio", "mizyun"],
          // Simulator actions (ios_install with `simulator`: install, launch, terminate, screenshot,
          // boot, shutdown) run without a card: Adam, 2026-11-12, "No cards for simulator" (ADR 0002,
          // "D4, simulator use"). "required" turns the cards back on. Builds, simulator builds
          // included, and device installs always ask. Left out, the plugin defaults to "required".
          simulatorCards: "off",
        },
      },
    },
  },
}
